/*


USED REGS

[E40000..E7FFFF] flashing space

RTC_ADDRESS = (ADDR:[FF8960] 
RTC_DATA =    (ADDR:[FF8962] 




[FF8964]  sets latched and stored into NVRAM ROM bank settings in NVRAM REGISTER 7F (FF wil also work as bit 8 is ignored).
This is the ROM FLASH BANK selects stored in NVRAM. These settings are loaded from NVRAM on machine RESET. 

xxABCDEF xxxxxxxx

A = PLD REGISTER ROM_DIS READ ONLY - READS ROM_DIS JUMPER, NOT ROM_DIS STORED IN NVRAM
B = PLD REGISTER OF FLASH SELECT 2 READ ONLY
C = PLD REGISTER OF FLASH SELECT 1 READ ONLY

D = PLD REGISTER ROM_DIS WRITE ONLY STORED IN NVRAM 
E = PLD REGISTER OF FLASH SELECT 2 STORED IN NVRAM 
F = PLD REGISTER OF FLASH SELECT 1 STORED IN NVRAM

x = don't care / write only 
11111 = command to enable the NVRAM updates (writing any zeros and the register will not be updated) 

NOTE - if bit "D" is HI, its the same as setting the physical jumper on the PCB to HI - it will boot from MB ROMS. 


[FF8966] "temp" FLASH BANK SELECTS WRITE ONLY
Because we can't swap ROM bank while ROM is running from flash, we need a second register which will override the first register. 
This allows us to swap bank versions for a single bus cycle, so the CPU just treats the bank as a simple address and wont crash the OS changing banks.


xxxxxxxx xxxxxxAB

A = PLD PROGRAMMING / STATUS REGISTER FOR FLASH BANK 2
B = PLD PROGRAMMING / STATUS REGISTER FOR FLASH BANK 1



*/





